# Example Motor Start Ladder Logic Documentation

## Network 1: Motor Start Circuit
```
|--[ Start PB ]--[ Stop PB ]--[ Motor Run ]--( Motor Output )--
```

## Network 2: Safety Interlock
```
|--[ Emergency Stop ]--[ Safety Relay ]--( Safety OK )--
```

## Network 3: Auto/Manual Mode
```
|--[ Auto Mode Selector ]--[ Auto Enable ]--( Auto Active )--
|--[ Manual Mode Selector ]--[ Manual Enable ]--( Manual Active )--
```

## Network 4: Speed Control
```
|--[ Speed Reference ]--[ Speed Controller ]--( Speed Output )--
```

## Description
This ladder logic documentation shows the basic motor control circuit including:
- Start/Stop control with latching
- Safety interlock with emergency stop
- Auto/Manual mode selection
- Speed control reference

## Tags Used
- Start_PB: BOOL - Start push button
- Stop_PB: BOOL - Stop push button
- Motor_Run: BOOL - Motor running status
- Motor_Output: BOOL - Motor control output
- Emergency_Stop: BOOL - Emergency stop input
- Safety_Relay: BOOL - Safety relay status
- Safety_OK: BOOL - Safety status output
- Auto_Mode_Selector: BOOL - Auto mode selector
- Auto_Enable: BOOL - Auto enable signal
- Auto_Active: BOOL - Auto mode active
- Manual_Mode_Selector: BOOL - Manual mode selector
- Manual_Enable: BOOL - Manual enable signal
- Manual_Active: BOOL - Manual mode active
- Speed_Reference: REAL - Speed reference value
- Speed_Controller: REAL - Speed controller output
- Speed_Output: REAL - Speed output to drive
